<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emmeline Pankhurst</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Emmeline Goulden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emmeline Pankhurst was a British political activist who led the militant campaign for women's suffrage. In 1903 she founded the Women's Social and Political Union, whose members, the suffragettes, turned from processions and heckling to window-smashing and arson, and she was imprisoned repeatedly. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> she suspended the campaign to support the war effort. She died in June 1928, weeks before Parliament gave women the vote on the same terms as men.</p></div>
